  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Are There Advantages To Replacing My Missing Teeth With Dental Implants In McLean, VA?\n\n\nSeptember 5, 2023\n\n\n#### Share This Post\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are a popular and effective long-term tooth replacement option for people who have one or more missing teeth. Depending on the number of teeth they are missing, and the number of dental implants they need to restore their smile, patients can get treated with single dental implants, implant supported dentures, and full mouth dental implants.\n\nInterested in learning more about the advantages of replacing missing teeth with dental implants? Continue reading to to find out more.\n\n\n## The Advantages To Replacing Missing Teeth With Dental Implants In McLean, VA\n\n\nBy getting treated with gold standard dental implants, the beauty, functionality, and health of people’s smiles are restored. Patients will even have a comfortable and anxiety-free dental implant procedure experience with the dental practice’s sedation dentistry options. The following are more detailed explanations of what the advantages of dental implants are:\n\n\n### Limits Jawbone Recession\n\n\nOne of the greatest advantages of dental implants, is their ability to limit jawbone recession and support facial bone structures. When a tooth is missing, the tooth root is no longer stimulating the jawbone. This lack of jawbone stimulation can lead to jawbone density loss over time, altering the persons facial structure and leading to them to having a more aged looking appearance.\n\nDental implants are made to act like natural tooth roots, stimulating the patients jawbone so that it is kept healthy and strong. With dental implants, patients can have a healthy and beautiful looking new smile.\n\n\n### Are Durable and Functional\n\n\nDental implants are made to be a durable and functional tooth replacement option. Specifically, dental implants can return over 99% of the durability and functionality of the patient’s natural teeth. Once the dental implants have been permanently placed in the patient’s jawbone, and the custom-made prosthesis is attached to them, patients will be able to eat, speak, and smile confidently for years to come.\n\n\n### Look, Feel, and Function Like Natural Teeth\n\n\nThe color, shape, and size of the prosthesis is custom made for patients’ dental implant procedures. With dental implants, patients can have a beautiful and natural looking new and improved smile. The best part is, with accurately placed dental implants, patients will be able to eat and speak with ease. By getting treated with personalized dental implants, patients will get natural looking, feeling, and functioning new teeth.\n\n\n### Easy To Maintain\n\n\nDental implants, much like natural teeth, require consistent and regular maintenance so that they can be healthy and successful for a long time. By regularly brushing and flossing their dental implants, as well as visiting a trusted dentist for teeth cleanings biannually, patients can keep their smile in great condition.\n\nBy getting treated with state-of-the-art-dental implants, patients will be able to maintain a normal diet, speak in comfort, and smile with ease and confidence. A skilled dental professional can predictably place a patient’s restorative dental implants with the latest techniques and technologies.\n\n\n## See Us Now So We Can Replace Your Missing Teeth With Dental Implants\n\n\nDo you have one or more missing teeth that you would like to replace with a proven tooth replacement procedure option? At our modern, caring, knowledgeable, and experienced office, you can get your missing teeth replaced with our quality dental implants. From single dental implants, to full mouth dental implants, we have the dental implant options to transform your smile.\n\nDon’t hesitate to improve your smile with us. Get in contact with Dr. Esam Nahlah and our exceptional team at our Dental Group of Tysons office to schedule an appointment today!\n\nPrevPreviousAre There Factors That Determine Which Type Of Dental Implant Procedure I Can Get Treated With?\n\nNextShould Sedation Dentistry Be Used For Full Mouth Dental Implant Procedures?Next\n\n\n#### More To Explore\n\n\n\n### Unlock the Benefits of Dental Implants: Your Best Teeth Replacement Option\n\n\nTooth loss can become an unfortunate reality for many as we age. Thankfully, advancements in dental technology, like dental implants,\n\nRead More »\n\nOctober 26, 2024\n\n\n### Your Comprehensive Guide on Dental Implants: The Best Replacement of Tooth Solution\n\n\nDental implants in McLean, VA are small, and titanium posts are surgically placed in your jawbone underneath your gum line.\n\nOctober 20, 2024\n\n\n## You Are Welcome Here.\n\n\nSchedule your consultation today.\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
